📉 Telecom Customer Churn & Retention Strategy Analytics

## 📌 Executive Project Summary
An end-to-end customer churn analysis and retention engineering project focused on identifying customer attrition drivers, high-risk contract segments, service stickiness impact, and revenue leakage.

This project combines SQL database transformations (Views, Tenure Bucketing, Stickiness Scoring) and an interactive Power BI Executive Dashboard featuring dynamic DAX insights and strategic action recommendations.

## 🛠️ Data Pipeline & Architecture

### 1. Data Cleaning & Feature Engineering (Excel / Power Query / SQL)
* Cleaned customer demographic data, handled missing values, and isolated core behavioral variables.
* Engineered custom analytical features inside MySQL using database Views (`v_Telecom_Churn_Final`):
  * **Binary Conversion:** Converted text churn statuses into numeric flags (`1/0`) for optimized DAX calculations.
  * **Tenure Grouping:** Categorized customer tenure into actionable cohorts (`0-1 Year`, `1-2 Years`, `2-4 Years`, `Over 4 Years`).
  * **Service Stickiness Score:** Aggregated active subscribed services (Phone, Internet, Online Security, Tech Support) into a single composite numerical score.

### 2. Database Engineering & SQL Analysis (MySQL)
* Conducted deep-dive exploratory data analysis (EDA):
  * **Payment Method Breakdown:** Computed churn rate percentages across payment methods to identify billing risk.
  * **High-Value At-Risk Filtering:** Identified non-churned high Monthly Charge customers on Month-to-Month contracts for proactive retention.
  * **Demographic Segmentation:** Evaluated churn impact across Senior Citizens and Online Security adoption.

---

## 📊 Dashboard Architecture & Interactive Visuals

The Power BI Dashboard features a high-contrast dark theme optimized for executive retention strategy discussions:

### 1️⃣ Core KPI Metrics
* **Total Customers:** Tracks overall customer base (7,032).
* **Churned Count & Revenue:** Real-time visibility into churned count and revenue impact (**$0.14M Churned Revenue**).
* **Churn Rate Gauge:** Displays the overall churn benchmark (**26.54%**).

### 2️⃣ Operational Risk Breakdown
* **Internet Service Type:** Horizontal bar chart highlighting higher attrition in **Fiber Optic (41.89%)** vs. **DSL (19.00%)**.
* **Contract Duration Impact:** Donut chart proving that **Month-to-Month contracts represent 88.55%** of total customer churn.
* **Tenure vs. Contract Trend:** Line chart depicting churn rate trajectory across monthly tenure cohorts.

### 3️⃣ Interactive Insights & Action Framework
* **Dynamic DAX Insights:** Real-time updating textual cards reflecting active filtered churn contributions.
* **Strategic Business Insights:** Formatted callout cards outlining concrete retention campaigns (e.g., offering 10% discounts for annual contract upgrades and performing technical audits on Fiber Optic latency).

---

## 🔑 Key Business Takeaways
* **Contract Vulnerability:** Month-to-Month customers represent nearly 88% of all churn, making contract upgrades the primary retention lever.
* **Service Quality Gap:** Fiber Optic subscribers show significantly higher churn rates (42%) compared to DSL, indicating potential service instability or pricing pressure.
* **Early Attrition Window:** Nearly 50% of customer loss occurs within the first 6 months of onboarding (`0-1 Year` tenure group).

---

